procedure.features:
This tender will be conducted using a two-stage 'competitive flexible' procedure.
The participation stage (stage one) will be used to shortlist which organisations we will invite to tender in the selection stage (stage two). The documents in this packet refer to this first stage as the 'Request to Participate' or 'RTP' stage.
We expect to invite up to five organisations for the second stage. If the scores of some applicants are the same or very close, we might choose to invite more than five organisations to tender. Further details can be found in the RTP instructions document.
The organisations selected for stage two will be sent the finalised 'Invitation to Tender' document pack through the Kent Business Portal. This will include a full set of instructions for stage two.
The versions of the ITT documents issued at this stage (stage one) are drafts only. At any time before the Tender Return Date, F&HDC may amend the ITT documents. All invited tenderers will be notified of any changes and F&HDC may choose to change the Tender Return Date to extend the deadline, if we consider this necessary.
Changes could include:
•	updated versions of appendices ITT appendices A-C;
•	additional appendices for your information;
•	updates to the tender timetable;
•	refinement of award criteria weightings without changing the order of importance;
•	refinement of the wording of questions in the draft ITT Supplier Response document without changing the overall subject of the questions; and 
•	any other minor changes which constitute refinement of the award criteria.
